WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:18.992
When Dr. Dolittle was a people doctor, he once helped a sick sailor.

2
00:00:18.993 --> 00:00:22.691
The sailor was very grateful to the doctor.

3
00:00:22.692 --> 00:00:26.867
"I will give you whatever you want," he promised.

4
00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:30.629
So Dr. Dolittle decided to ask for his help.

5
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.819
"I need to travel to Africa," he said.

6
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:39.401
"You may use my boat," the sailor answered.

7
00:00:39.402 --> 00:00:44.223
Soon Dr. Dolittle was ready for the great journey to Africa.

8
00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:47.826
He felt excited and sad at the same time.

9
00:00:47.827 --> 00:00:52.854
He could not take all the animals with him.

10
00:00:52.855 --> 00:00:57.054
"Take care of the house," he said to the remaining animals.

11
00:00:57.055 --> 00:01:00.529
"Stay warm and drink lots of water."

12
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:08.706
"We'll miss you, Dr. Dolittle," the animals cried.

13
00:01:08.707 --> 00:01:11.600
For six long weeks, they sailed.

14
00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:15.779
Polynesia and Chee-Chee enjoyed the sun and the ocean.

15
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.139
"Can you see Africa yet?" the monkey asked.

16
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.132
"Not yet, Chee-Chee, but soon," answered the doctor.

17
00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:29.324
The parrot and the monkey were so excited to return to Africa, their home.

18
00:01:29.325 --> 00:01:33.363
However, the others were not enjoying themselves too much.

19
00:01:33.364 --> 00:01:38.033
"Oh, I feel so sick," the green pig moaned.

20
00:01:38.034 --> 00:01:46.973
"Don't get sick on me!" growled Jip.

21
00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:52.284
"It's too bad you can't swim," Dab-Dab jumped onto the boat.

22
00:01:52.285 --> 00:01:54.925
"The water is so warm today."

23
00:01:54.926 --> 00:02:01.875
"Hey! Watch it!" Too-Too did not like water at all.

24
00:02:01.876 --> 00:02:07.416
John Dolittle was a good doctor, but not a good sailor.

25
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:10.999
"I'm afraid we're lost," he said one morning.

26
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.914
"Yoo-hoo!"

27
00:02:12.915 --> 00:02:16.824
"What was that?" asked Gub-Gub.

28
00:02:16.825 --> 00:02:17.998
"What was what?

29
00:02:17.999 --> 00:02:21.107
I didn't hear anything!" growled Jip.

30
00:02:21.108 --> 00:02:23.531
"Oh, yoo-hoo!"

31
00:02:23.532 --> 00:02:27.482
"Look! Over there!" shouted Dab-Dab.

32
00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:31.204
The sound was coming from two dolphins.

33
00:02:31.205 --> 00:02:35.218
"Are you Dr. Dolittle?" called out one dolphin.

34
00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:40.663
"Yes, I am. How did you know?" Dr. Dolittle asked, surprised.

35
00:02:40.664 --> 00:02:42.734
"We heard all about you, Doctor.

36
00:02:42.735 --> 00:02:47.947
You're famous!" shouted the other one.

37
00:02:47.948 --> 00:02:51.762
"We must get to Africa," said Chee-Chee.

38
00:02:51.763 --> 00:02:56.043
"We know. We'll help you get there," said the first dolphin.

39
00:02:56.044 --> 00:02:59.854
"Just follow us!" said the other.

40
00:02:59.855 --> 00:03:06.320
"I bet I could swim faster than them!" Dab-Dab said with a sniff.

41
00:03:06.321 --> 00:03:10.784
The dolphins guided Dr. Dolittle's boat across the ocean.

42
00:03:10.785 --> 00:03:16.254
As they passed by, fish and whales swam up to see the animal doctor.

43
00:03:16.255 --> 00:03:21.293
"That's the human who speaks our language!" whispered a large fish.

44
00:03:21.294 --> 00:03:26.676
"He's going to save the monkeys!" shouted the whale.

45
00:03:26.677 --> 00:03:30.433
Finally it was time for the dolphins to leave them.

46
00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:34.651
"This is as far as we can go," one dolphin said.

47
00:03:34.652 --> 00:03:39.831
"Just keep going straight and you'll see land," the other said.

48
00:03:39.832 --> 00:03:43.857
"How can we ever thank you?" asked Dr. Dolittle.

49
00:03:43.858 --> 00:03:46.411
"Save the monkeys, Doctor."

50
00:03:46.412 --> 00:03:52.189
The dolphins swam away into the sunset.

51
00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.086
That night, there was a terrible storm.

52
00:03:55.087 --> 00:03:58.214
The waves carried the boat in every direction.

53
00:03:58.215 --> 00:04:05.066
"Oh, I'm going to be sick," Gub-Gub, who was greener than ever, moaned.

54
00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:09.663
"Hold on tight!" shouted Jip.

55
00:04:09.664 --> 00:04:12.702
The wind howled and the sky roared.

56
00:04:12.703 --> 00:04:18.099
"Are we ever going to make it to Africa?" cried Chee-Chee.

57
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.275
Suddenly the boat hit something hard.

58
00:04:21.276 --> 00:04:24.999
Water began to fill the boat.

59
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.880
"Jump off! Jump off!" shouted Jip.

60
00:04:28.881 --> 00:04:33.960
"Doctor! We're almost on land!" Too-Too pointed.

61
00:04:33.961 --> 00:04:39.290
"Quick! Dab-Dab! Take this rope!" Polynesia commanded.

62
00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:44.692
"Tie it around that tree!"

63
00:04:44.693 --> 00:04:49.690
One by one, the animals and Dr. Dolittle crossed to land.

64
00:04:49.691 --> 00:04:52.971
They watched as the water swallowed up their boat.

65
00:04:52.972 --> 00:04:57.763
"We don't have a boat anymore," Gub-Gub said sadly.

66
00:04:57.764 --> 00:05:05.730
"But we're alive. That's the most important thing," Dr. Dolittle smiled.
